{"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":0,"metadata":{"colab":{"provenance":[]},"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"Python 3"},"language_info":{"name":"python"}},"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["\n","\n","---\n","\n","## Problem Statement\n","\n","**Perform a two-sample t-test on the following data:**\n","\n","* **Data 1:** \\[18.4, 19.1, 17.9, 18.7, 18.3]\n","* **Data 2:** \\[20.2, 20.5, 20.1, 20.3, 20.4]\n","\n","Use significance level **α = 0.05** to determine whether the population means differ.\n","\n","### Tasks\n","\n","1. State $H_0$ and $H_1$. You will assume **equal variances** (pooled).\n","2. Compute the **sample means**, **sample variances (ddof = 1)**, and the **mean difference**.\n","3. Calculate the **t-statistic**, **degrees of freedom**, and the **two-tailed p-value**.\n","4. Construct the **95% confidence interval** for the mean difference.\n","5. **Decision & Interpretation:** Conclude (reject / fail to reject $H_0$) and explain the result **in one or two plain-English sentences**.\n","\n","\n","\n","---\n","\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"isTJJjIqEVMq"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"f30425ea"},"source":["### Task 1: State $H_0$ and $H_1$\n","\n","*   **Null Hypothesis ($H_0$):** There is no significant difference between the population means of the two datasets ($\\mu_1 = \\mu_2$).\n","*   **Alternative Hypothesis ($H_1$):** There is a significant difference between the population means of the two datasets ($\\mu_1 \\neq \\mu_2$).\n","\n","We assume equal variances (pooled t-test)."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"f87abb61"},"source":["### Task 2: Define the datasets and compute sample statistics"]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import random\n","import numpy as np\n","import math\n","import scipy.stats as stats"],"metadata":{"id":"MBiQoMP78xkY"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"N53R_bNm3qZR"}},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"971cb442","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1788685367309,"user_tz":-360,"elapsed":11,"user":{"displayName":"Rimon Chandra Bhowmik","userId":"05613841205344715165"}},"outputId":"fb94b305-d979-42b0-954f-d57a28badebc"},"source":["# Define the new datasets\n","data1_new = np.array([18.4, 19.1, 17.9, 18.7, 18.3])\n","data2_new = np.array([20.2, 20.5, 20.1, 20.3, 20.4])\n","\n","# Compute sample means\n","mean1_new = np.mean(data1_new)\n","mean2_new = np.mean(data2_new)\n","\n","# Compute sample variances (ddof=1 for sample variance)\n","s1_sq_new = np.var(data1_new, ddof=1)\n","s2_sq_new = np.var(data2_new, ddof=1)\n","\n","# Compute mean difference\n","mean_diff_new = mean1_new - mean2_new\n","\n","print(f\"Sample 1 Mean: {mean1_new:.2f}\")\n","print(f\"Sample 2 Mean: {mean2_new:.2f}\")\n","print(f\"Sample 1 Variance: {s1_sq_new:.2f}\")\n","print(f\"Sample 2 Variance: {s2_sq_new:.2f}\")\n","print(f\"Mean Difference (Sample 1 - Sample 2): {mean_diff_new:.2f}\")"],"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Sample 1 Mean: 18.48\n","Sample 2 Mean: 20.30\n","Sample 1 Variance: 0.20\n","Sample 2 Variance: 0.02\n","Mean Difference (Sample 1 - Sample 2): -1.82\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"0f473c0e"},"source":["### Task 3: Calculate t-statistic, degrees of freedom, and p-value"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"b47d521a","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1788685367320,"user_tz":-360,"elapsed":10,"user":{"displayName":"Rimon Chandra Bhowmik","userId":"05613841205344715165"}},"outputId":"8799f547-2ac7-4b67-eb4c-631839dd38d9"},"source":["\n","\n","# Perform the two-sample t-test assuming equal variances\n","t_statistic_new, p_value_new = stats.ttest_ind(data1_new, data2_new, equal_var=True)\n","\n","# Degrees of freedom\n","n1_new, n2_new = len(data1_new), len(data2_new)\n","df_new = n1_new + n2_new - 2\n","\n","print(f\"t-Statistic: {t_statistic_new:.3f}\")\n","print(f\"Degrees of Freedom: {df_new}\")\n","print(f\"p-Value: {p_value_new:.4f}\")"],"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["t-Statistic: -8.542\n","Degrees of Freedom: 8\n","p-Value: 0.0000\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"299d7676"},"source":["### Task 4: Construct the 95% confidence interval for the mean difference"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"33906464","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1788685367330,"user_tz":-360,"elapsed":10,"user":{"displayName":"Rimon Chandra Bhowmik","userId":"05613841205344715165"}},"outputId":"0ddd7f7d-1025-418f-d5b6-c98f02feac68"},"source":["# Pooled variance for confidence interval calculation\n","sp_sq_new = ((n1_new - 1) * s1_sq_new + (n2_new - 1) * s2_sq_new) / (n1_new + n2_new - 2)\n","\n","# Standard error using pooled variance\n","std_err_new = np.sqrt(sp_sq_new * (1/n1_new + 1/n2_new))\n","\n","# 95% confidence interval for the mean difference\n","ci_new = stats.t.interval(0.95, df_new, loc=mean_diff_new, scale=std_err_new)\n","\n","print(f\"95% Confidence Interval of Mean Difference: [{ci_new[0]:.3f}, {ci_new[1]:.3f}]\")"],"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["95% Confidence Interval of Mean Difference: [-2.311, -1.329]\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"fd016989"},"source":["### Task 5: Decision & Interpretation"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"41958ba1","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1788685367508,"user_tz":-360,"elapsed":170,"user":{"displayName":"Rimon Chandra Bhowmik","userId":"05613841205344715165"}},"outputId":"9506c47f-2127-47a1-c102-50d1447eb8e2"},"source":["alpha_new = 0.05  # Significance level\n","\n","if p_value_new < alpha_new:\n","    print(\"Decision: Reject the null hypothesis.\")\n","    print(\"Interpretation: Based on the t-test results, there is a statistically significant difference between the population means of the two datasets at the 0.05 significance level.\")\n","else:\n","    print(\"Decision: Fail to reject the null hypothesis.\")\n","    print(\"Interpretation: Based on the t-test results, there is no statistically significant difference between the population means of the two datasets at the 0.05 significance level.\")"],"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Decision: Reject the null hypothesis.\n","Interpretation: Based on the t-test results, there is a statistically significant difference between the population means of the two datasets at the 0.05 significance level.\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"code","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"AdDo_2AfrMlC"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]}]}